note ham/ngrun-hostwords-4 (omc 564c5835 exec argv limits): a well-formed execprog packet of 65537 bytes (count 1,
note one record of 65533 bytes), one past the 65536-byte cap of an exec argument packet, traps 3 on its length
note before any kernel call (OMEGESE s10); ngrun refuses execprog (115) only after that check. Every other packet
note rule holds, so only the byte cap can trap (bay 3 review of 2d6ed949: a zero-filled packet also traps on its
note count 0 and did not pin the cap).
fn main to int
a = new uchar 65537 120
put a 0 1
put a 1 0
put a 2 253
put a 3 255
k = execprog a 0 65537
ret int and k 255
end
